given-names>NH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Proactive administration of platelets and plasma for patients with a ruptured abdominal aortic aneurysm: evaluating a change in transfusion practice</article-title><source>Transfusion</source><year>2007</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>593</fpage><lpage>598</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17381616</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Belsley</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessing the presence of harmful collinearity and other forms of weak data through a test for signal-to-noise</article-title><source>J Econome</source><year>1982</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>211</fpage><lpage>253</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hellstern</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Haubelt</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Indications for plasma in massive transfusion</article-title><source>Thromb Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>107</volume><fpage>S19</fpage><lpage>S22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12379288</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johansson</surname><given-names>PI</given-names></name><name><surname>Bochsen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Stensballe</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Secher</surname><given-names>NH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transfusion packages for massively bleeding patients: the effect on clot formation and stability as evaluated by Thrombelastograph (TEG&#x000ae;)</article-title><source>Transfus Apher Sci</source><year>2008</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>8</lpa